# AGENTS.md

This file provides guidance to AI coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, etc.) when working with code in this repository.

## Project Overview

- Primary Language: Go (see `go.mod` for version requirement)
- Main Branch: `main`
- Current Version: See `VERSION`

## Shared Skills

- Run `make skills` to install or update grpc-kit shared skills under `scripts/skills/skills`.
- When a task matches a shared skill, read its complete `SKILL.md` before acting and follow any referenced resources it requires.
- For release notes, version summaries, or CHANGELOG updates, use `scripts/skills/skills/generate-release-changelog/SKILL.md`.
- If the shared skill directory is unavailable, report that it has not been initialized before falling back to repository conventions.

## Service Skills

- Service-specific skills live in `.agents/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`. When a task matches one, read its complete `SKILL.md` and only the supporting resources relevant to the task before acting.
- Available service skill: `add-api-domain` — add a versioned API domain, HTTP mappings, handler implementation, and API tests. Read `.agents/skills/add-api-domain/SKILL.md` for that work.
- See `.agents/skills/README.md` for the format and maintenance rules. Native support and refresh behavior vary by client; agents without native discovery can read the indexed file directly.
- Service skills are independent of shared skills. Do not run `make skills`, access the network, or modify the `scripts/skills` submodule merely to use a service skill.
- Give service skills distinct names. If a name collides with another scope, use the explicit repository path rather than assuming a client-specific precedence rule.
- These files are business-editable. When adding or removing a service skill, update the compact index above.

## Repository Structure

```text
api/
cmd/
config/
handler/
modeler/
scripts/
test/e2e/
docs/
web/admin/
deploy/
```

Key Files:

- `go.mod` - Go version and dependencies
- `Makefile` - Build system (see `make help`)
- `scripts/generate.sh` - Proto/Ent code generation entrypoint
- `scripts/env` - Build and generation metadata (`PRODUCT_CODE`, `SHORT_NAME`, `API_VERSION`)

Directory Responsibilities:

- `api/{{ .Global.ProductCode }}/{{ .Global.ShortName }}/{{ .Template.Service.APIVersion }}` - API contracts (`*.proto`) and generated RPC bindings (`*.pb.go`, `*_grpc.pb.go`, `*.pb.gw.go`)
- `cmd/server/` - service bootstrap entrypoint (generated by grpc-kit scaffolding)
- `handler/` - RPC registration and service handlers
- `modeler/` - data models, flow logic, and ent schema/runtime
- `config/` - runtime configuration files for local/minimal environments
- `scripts/` - generation, environment checks, packaging, and helper automation
- `test/e2e/` - black-box API end-to-end tests (`//go:build e2e`), see `test/e2e/README.md`
- `docs/` - design, migration, and feature documentation
- `web/admin/` - frontend admin application

## Build System

```shell
make build
```

Key Makefile Targets: `make help` for full list

Recommended Workflow (source of truth: `Makefile`):

```shell
make precheck
make generate
make test
make build
```

- Use `make run` for local service startup.
- Avoid bypassing Makefile targets when adding or changing API/model code.

## Testing

- Default validation target is `make test` (includes `make generate` and `go test ./...`).
- Use `make lint` to run formatting and vet checks before submitting larger changes.
- If API contracts or ent schema change, run generation first and include generated artifacts in the same change.
- Unit and integration tests stay colocated with the source they cover; never move them into `test/`.
- Black-box API e2e tests live in per-domain packages under `test/e2e/`, are all guarded by
  `//go:build e2e`, and run with `make test-e2e` against a locally running server (`make run`).
  Directory conventions, naming rules, and environment variables: `test/e2e/README.md`.
- Purity constraint for `test/e2e/`: import only the standard library, `test/e2e/client`, and
  `test/e2e/fixture`. Importing `api/`, `handler/`, `internal/`, or `modeler/` is forbidden —
  e2e asserts the external HTTP contract, not internal implementation.
- `test/e2e/demo/` covers the built-in sample endpoints. Delete it together with
  `handler/rpc_demo.go` and `api/**/demo.proto` when the sample API is removed.

## Configuration

- Local runtime config is passed via `-c`, defaulting to `./config/app.yaml` in `cmd/server/main.go`.
- For local development, use `make run`, which starts with `config/app-dev-local.yaml`.
- Keep environment-specific config in `config/`; do not hardcode runtime values into handlers/modelers.

## Development Patterns

- API design in the `api/` directory must comply with the [Google API Improvement Proposals (AIP)](https://google.aip.dev/).
- Keep API versioned under `api/{{ .Global.ProductCode }}/{{ .Global.ShortName }}/{{ .Template.Service.APIVersion }}/`; register cross-domain RPCs through `microservice.proto`.
- For API changes: update `*.proto` plus gateway/openapi configs first, then run `make generate`.

## Git Commit Convention

- All commit messages must follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).
- Use the format: `type(scope)!: short summary`
- Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.
- Use `!` (or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer) for breaking changes.
- Keep the subject concise and imperative; avoid trailing periods.

Examples:

- `feat(handler): add batch ipam allocation endpoint`
- `fix(modeler): handle empty opensearch result safely`
- `docs(readme): clarify local run prerequisites`
- `refactor(rpc_search)!: rename query fields for aip compliance`

When a change affects generated artifacts, include source and generated files in the same commit message scope when possible.

## Generated Files Policy

Files in this project fall into two categories, distinguished by whether the first line contains `// Code generated by "grpc-kit-cli/...". DO NOT EDIT.`:

- Framework-managed files (with `DO NOT EDIT` header): Managed by grpc-kit CLI, overwritten on `grpc-kit-cli update`. Do not modify. Examples: `cmd/server/main.go`, `handler/register.go`, `handler/microservice.go`, `api/${{ .Global.ProductCode }}/{{ .Global.ShortName }}/{{ .Template.Service.APIVersion }}/*.pb.go`, `api/{{ .Global.ProductCode }}/{{ .Global.ShortName }}/{{ .Template.Service.APIVersion }}/microservice.pb.gw.go`.
- Business-editable files (no `DO NOT EDIT` header): Preserved on upgrade, free to modify. Examples: `handler/private.go`, `handler/rpc_demo.go`, `modeler/mcp/registrar.go`, `modeler/mcp/registrar_test.go`, `config/app-dev-local.yaml`, `test/e2e/**`.

Additional rules:

- Do not manually edit framework-managed files. If generated output is incorrect, fix source definitions (`*.proto`, gateway/openapi config, ent schema) and regenerate via `scripts/generate.sh`.
- Generated OpenAPI output is produced by `scripts/generate.sh` and moved to `public/openapi/`.
- Place custom business logic (HTTP routes, MCP resource registration, RPC handler implementations) in business-editable files (e.g., `handler/private.go`). Framework-managed files provide extension hooks such as `privateHTTPHandle(mux)` and `privateMCPHandle()`.

## Environment and Dependency Notes

- `GOPATH` must be configured before running Make targets (`scripts/precheck.sh` enforces this).
- Keep `go.mod` `replace` entries intact unless the user explicitly asks to change local dependency mapping.
